---
// src/pages/about.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About VerseSEO — Why We Exist"
  description="VerseSEO exists to give small businesses, SaaS founders, and creators the visibility intelligence they need to compete in modern search and AI."
  canonical="https://verseseo.com/about"
>
  <Navbar />

  <main class="flex-1">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 sm:py-20">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight mb-2">About VerseSEO</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-10">Visibility intelligence for the modern web</p>

      <div class="prose prose-slate prose-sm max-w-none space-y-8 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">Why VerseSEO Exists</h2>
          <p>Search has fragmented. Your customers don't just search on Google anymore — they ask ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, and Reddit. Meanwhile, small businesses and indie creators are stuck using SEO tools built for a world that no longer exists.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">VerseSEO was built to solve this problem. We give small businesses, SaaS founders, and creators a single place to understand their visibility across every surface where people discover products and answers — traditional search, AI answer engines, and community platforms like Reddit.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">The Problem We're Solving</h2>
          <p>Most SEO tools are either too complex for small teams or too narrow to cover the full picture. They focus on Google alone and miss the growing role of AI-generated answers, Reddit threads, and other discovery surfaces.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">At the same time, the tactics many people use — mass Reddit posting, AI-generated comments, keyword stuffing — are increasingly punished by platforms and ignored by AI engines. The old playbook is broken.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">VerseSEO takes a different approach: help you understand where you're visible, where you're missing, and where you can genuinely provide value.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">What VerseSEO Does</h2>
          <p>VerseSEO is a lightweight visibility platform that covers five core areas:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li><strong>Technical Website Health</strong> — Crawl your site for SEO issues, broken links, and technical problems.</li>
            <li><strong>Search & Intent Discovery</strong> — Find high-intent keywords and search opportunities you're missing.</li>
            <li><strong>Reddit Opportunity Listening</strong> — Discover relevant Reddit conversations where you can genuinely help.</li>
            <li><strong>AI/LLM Visibility</strong> — Track how your brand appears (or doesn't) in ChatGPT, Claude, and Perplexity.</li>
            <li><strong>Content Engine</strong> — Generate briefs and content optimized for both search and AI answer engines.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">Who It's Built For</h2>
          <p>VerseSEO is designed for:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li>Small businesses that need actionable SEO insights without enterprise complexity</li>
            <li>SaaS founders and indie hackers building in public</li>
            <li>Creators and content producers who want to be found across search and AI platforms</li>
            <li>Anyone who wants to compete on visibility without a large marketing team</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">Our Approach</h2>
          <p>We believe the future of visibility is about being genuinely helpful, not gaming algorithms. VerseSEO is built around three principles:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li><strong>Real data over guesses</strong> — Every insight is based on actual crawl data, search results, and AI engine outputs.</li>
            <li><strong>Authenticity over manipulation</strong> — We help you find opportunities to contribute value, not to spam or fake engagement.</li>
            <li><strong>Simplicity over bloat</strong> — We focus on the actions that move the needle, without overwhelming you with dashboards.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">Where We Are</h2>
          <p>VerseSEO is an early-stage product built by a small team. We're actively developing the platform, shipping features, and improving based on user feedback. We're not a large company with a massive team — we're builders solving a problem we care about.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">If you have questions, feedback, or want to connect, reach us at <a href="mailto:support@verseseo.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@verseseo.com</a>.</p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
